/*!
\page page_stbtofrawhit StBTofRawHit

\brief Raw TDC hit from the STAR Barrel Time-of-Flight (BTOF) DAQ stream.

\section btofrawhit_overview Overview

StBTofRawHit stores a single raw TDC hit from the BTOF DAQ stream before any calibration.
Each object corresponds to one TDC edge (leading or trailing) recorded by the HPTDC/TDIG
electronics on a given BTOF tray fiber.

The BTOF system, operational since Run 8 (2007), reads out 120 trays via four fibers.
The edge type is encoded in the sign of \c mFlag (positive = leading, negative = trailing);
the magnitude minus one gives the fiber ID (0–3).

Raw hits are stored in \ref StBTofCollection via StEvent::btofCollection().

\section btofrawhit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
TObject → StObject → StBTofRawHit
\endcode

\section btofrawhit_members Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| mFlag | Char_t | Edge flag: +ve = leading, −ve = trailing; \|flag\|−1 = fiberId |
| mTray | UChar_t | Tray number (1–120) |
| mChannel | UChar_t | TDC channel within the tray electronics |
| mTdc | UInt_t | Raw TDC count (bin number; ~24.4 ps/bin) |

\section btofrawhit_methods Key Methods

- flag() — raw flag byte
- leadingEdge() — true if leading-edge hit
- trailingEdge() — true if trailing-edge hit
- fiberId() — fiber ID derived from flag (0–3)
- tray() — tray number (1–120)
- channel() — TDC channel number
- tdc() — raw TDC count

\section btofrawhit_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StBTofCollection* coll = event->btofCollection();
if (coll) {
    const StSPtrVecBTofRawHit& rawHits = coll->tofRawHits();
    for (const auto& r : rawHits) {
        int  tray   = r->tray();
        int  chan   = r->channel();
        bool isLE   = r->leadingEdge();
        int  fiber  = r->fiberId();   // 0–3
        // ~24.4 ps/bin
        double approxNs = r->tdc() * 24.4e-3;
    }
}
\endcode

\see StBTofHit, StBTofHeader, StBTofCollection
*/
